<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related Work</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Streaming LLMs</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Streaming LLMs <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al. (2026a)</a></cite> aim to move language-model inference from static full-context processing toward dynamic interaction, where input perception, reasoning, output generation, and external actions may overlap. From an application perspective, existing work has explored several forms of real-time interaction. Simultaneous translation studies <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">read while outputting</em>, where models learn or impose read/write policies such as wait-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and efficient interaction decision to trade source completeness for latency <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2018</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arivazhagan et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Elbayad et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al., 2026b</a>)</cite>, with recent LLM-based and speech-to-speech systems extending this setting to real-time translation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Agostinelli et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Raffel et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Streaming video and multimodal systems study <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">think/speak while watching</em>, processing frames incrementally, chatting over evolving video streams, or generating reasoning synchronized with incoming visual evidence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al., 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2026</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2026</a>)</cite>. Spoken dialogue systems study <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">think while hearing</em> and <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">speak while thinking</em>, enabling low-latency or full-duplex speech interaction and, in some cases, hidden reasoning during listening or speaking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie and Wu, 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Défossez et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fang et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chiang et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2026b</a>)</cite>. Agentic systems further study <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">think while acting</em>, where models interleave reasoning with tool use, retrieval, function calls, or anticipatory actions under streaming observations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu and Clune, 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gim et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al., 2025a</a>)</cite>. These scenarios show that streaming LLMs are motivated not only by faster token emission, but also by the need to coordinate computation with continuously evolving inputs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Among these scenarios, <em id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">think while reading</em> provides a clean abstraction for streaming reasoning, where the model processes input segments sequentially, reasons under partial observations, and performs final deliberation after the stream ends. StreamingThinker <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tong et al., 2025a</a>)</cite> realizes this paradigm with sentence-level streaming CoT and streaming-specific attention, position encoding, and KV-cache designs, showing how LLMs can reason under streaming visibility constraints. Yet its intermediate reasoning behavior is largely shaped by constructed supervised traces. AdaSR instead studies whether models can learn their own computation policy: when to think, when to skip, and how to allocate computation between online thoughts and final deep reasoning.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Policy Optimization in RLVR</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR) has recently become a
central paradigm for improving the reasoning ability of large language models,
where policies are optimized using automatically checkable outcome rewards rather
than learned reward models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">DeepSeek-AI, 2025</a>)</cite>.
Early RLHF and RLVR systems commonly build upon PPO-style clipped policy
objectives <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>; <a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ziegler et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ouyang et al., 2022</a>)</cite>,
while GRPO replaces the critic with group-relative reward normalization,
estimating the baseline from multiple rollouts of the same prompt and thereby
reducing the cost of value modeling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shao et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Recent studies
further refine this paradigm from different perspectives. REINFORCE-style
methods revisit critic-free optimization for language-model
alignment <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ahmadian et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. Dr. GRPO analyzes the optimization bias of GRPO and
shows that length-dependent loss aggregation can artificially encourage longer
responses, especially for incorrect trajectories; it therefore modifies the
aggregation and normalization scheme to improve token efficiency while preserving
reasoning performance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. DAPO improves the
scalability and stability of long-CoT RL by introducing decoupled clipping and
dynamic sampling, together with practical techniques such as Clip-Higher,
token-level policy-gradient loss, and overlong reward shaping <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
GDPO extends GRPO to multi-reward RLVR by decoupling the normalization of
different reward components before aggregation, alleviating advantage collapse
caused by directly normalizing summed rewards <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2026a</a>)</cite>. Beyond
text-only reasoning, PAPO incorporates perception-aware optimization into RLVR by
adding an implicit perception loss and entropy regularization, enabling GRPO- or
DAPO-style training to better support multimodal
reasoning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Overall, these methods improve RLVR along
dimensions such as critic-free optimization, length-bias correction, training
stability, multi-reward composition, and multimodal grounding. However, they
still largely optimize completed trajectories at the sequence or token level,
without explicitly modeling the hierarchical temporal structure of streaming
reasoning. In contrast, our HRPO targets the phase-structured credit assignment
problem, assigning advantages over streaming, deep-reasoning, and global token
ranges to better optimize adaptive reasoning under partial and evolving inputs.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>HRPO Analysis</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">GRPO Limitation for Streaming Reasoning</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We further formalize why the standard GRPO objective in
Eq. <a href="#S2.E2" title="In GRPO for Reasoning ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> is mismatched with streaming reasoning. For a sampled
streaming trajectory <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o_{i}=[R_{1},\ldots,R_{T},R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o_{i}=[R_{1},\ldots,R_{T},R]</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\mathrm{bnd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>bnd</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\mathrm{bnd}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote
the boundary between the online streaming phase and the final deep-thinking
phase, as defined in Eq. <a href="#S2.E1" title="In Streaming Thinking ‣ 2 Preliminary ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. GRPO first collapses the whole
trajectory into a scalar reward <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and then assigns the resulting
group-normalized advantage <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to every token:</p>
<table id="A2.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{GRPO}}(\theta)\propto\mathbb{E}\!\Bigg[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>GRPO</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∝</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{GRPO}}(\theta)\propto\mathbb{E}\!\Bigg[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}m_{i,t}r_{i,t}\hat{A}_{i}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right)\Bigg]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mi>m</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}m_{i,t}r_{i,t}\hat{A}_{i}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right)\Bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes whether the clipped surrogate is active. Thus tokens
before and after <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{\mathrm{bnd}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>bnd</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{\mathrm{bnd}}</annotation></semantics></math> receive the same learning signal even
though they play different roles: streaming tokens should be judged by the
quality and timeliness of partial-observation reasoning, while deep tokens
should be judged by full-context integration. <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">This flat credit assignment creates two failure modes.</span> If an incorrect or unhelpful streaming segment is rescued by deep deliberation, GRPO still reinforces the streaming tokens
because the final reward is high; conversely, useful streaming thoughts are
penalized whenever the final answer fails for reasons in the deep phase.
Consequently, GRPO cannot tell whether performance changes come from online
reasoning, final deliberation, or their interaction, motivating the
hierarchical advantage decomposition used by HRPO.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Advantage Decomposition and Policy Gradient</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We keep the notation in Eq. <a href="#S3.E5" title="In Policy Optimization Objective ‣ 3.1 Hierarchical Relative Policy Optimization ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>. Starting from the original HRPO
objective, the local and global surrogate terms can be grouped by token time step. Streaming tokens receive the streaming local signal and the global signal; deep tokens receive the deep local signal and the same global signal:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E10X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{HRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D}\\
\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\end{subarray}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Bigg[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>HRPO</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{HRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D}\\
\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\end{subarray}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Bigg[</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="9" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\resizebox{22609920}{}{$\displaystyle\underbrace{\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\mathcal{C}(r_{i,t}^{s},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s})+\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=|t_{\mathrm{s}}|+1}^{|o_{i}|}\mathcal{C}(r_{i,t}^{d},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{local clipped surrogate objective}\end{subarray}}$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mpadded style="width:345.0pt;height:46.3pt;vertical-align:-25.0pt;" depth="25.0pt" height="21.3pt" width="345.0pt"><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtable><mtr><mtd><mtext>local clipped surrogate objective</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder></mpadded><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\resizebox{22609920}{}{$\displaystyle\underbrace{\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\mathcal{C}(r_{i,t}^{s},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s})+\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=|t_{\mathrm{s}}|+1}^{|o_{i}|}\mathcal{C}(r_{i,t}^{d},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{local clipped surrogate objective}\end{subarray}}$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\resizebox{22609920}{}{$\displaystyle+\underbrace{\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\Bigg(\mathcal{C}(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{global clipped surrogate objective}\end{subarray}}-\beta\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\pi_{\theta}\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\Bigg)\Bigg]\Bigg\}$}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mpadded style="width:345.0pt;height:43.9pt;vertical-align:-13.0pt;" depth="13.0pt" height="30.9pt" width="345.0pt"><mo>+</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mtext>global clipped surrogate objective</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mpadded><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\resizebox{22609920}{}{$\displaystyle+\underbrace{\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\Bigg(\mathcal{C}(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g})}_{\begin{subarray}{c}\text{global clipped surrogate objective}\end{subarray}}-\beta\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\pi_{\theta}\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}\right)\Bigg)\Bigg]\Bigg\}$}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D}\\
\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\end{subarray}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Bigg[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D}\\
\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\end{subarray}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Bigg[</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\Bigg(\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{s},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}\right)+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t=1}^{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\Bigg(\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{s},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}\right)+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\beta}{|o_{i}|}\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\beta}{|o_{i}|}\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xf" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xf.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{t=|t_{\mathrm{s}}|+1}^{|o_{i}|}\Bigg(\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{d},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{t=|t_{\mathrm{s}}|+1}^{|o_{i}|}\Bigg(\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{d},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xg" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xg.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)-\frac{\beta}{|o_{i}|}\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msup><mo>)</mo><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)-\frac{\beta}{|o_{i}|}\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E10Xh" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E10Xh.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg)\Bigg]\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg)\Bigg]\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This time-wise form makes the effective credit assignment explicit: before
the boundary <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|t_{\text{s}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|t_{\text{s}}|</annotation></semantics></math>, each token is optimized with a streaming-local
coefficient <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda/|t_{\text{s}}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda/|t_{\text{s}}|</annotation></semantics></math> and a global coefficient <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/|o_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/|o_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>; after
the boundary, the streaming-local term is replaced by the deep-local
coefficient <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda/(|o_{i}|\!-\!|t_{\text{s}}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda/(|o_{i}|\!-\!|t_{\text{s}}|)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.5" class="ltx_p">We next derive the corresponding policy gradient. By linearity of
differentiation and expectation,</p>
<table id="A2.E11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E11X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{HRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D}\\
\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\end{subarray}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Bigg[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>HRPO</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></msub><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">[</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{HRPO}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\begin{subarray}{c}(q,a)\sim\mathcal{D}\\
\{o_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta_{\mathrm{old}}}\end{subarray}}\Bigg\{\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\Bigg[</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="6" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{s},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{s},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=|t_{\mathrm{s}}|+1}^{|o_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{d},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\mathrm{s}}|}\sum_{t=|t_{\mathrm{s}}|+1}^{|o_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{d},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>g</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{g},\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{\beta}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:1.431em;" width="1.431em"><mi>KL</mi></mpadded><mo>(</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{\beta}{|o_{i}|}\sum_{t=1}^{|o_{i}|}\nabla_{\theta}\operatorname{KL}\!\left(\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E11Xe" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E11Xe.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg]\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg]\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.6" class="ltx_p">For each <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{s,d,g\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{s,d,g\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the sampled
advantage <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and the old-policy denominator in
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i,t}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i,t}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed with respect to <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, so</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}r_{i,t}^{\ell}=r_{i,t}^{\ell}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{i,t}|q,o_{i,&lt;t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}r_{i,t}^{\ell}=r_{i,t}^{\ell}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(o_{i,t}|q,o_{i,&lt;t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.7" class="ltx_p">Therefore the clipped surrogate contributes a policy-gradient term only when
the unclipped PPO branch is selected:</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{\ell},\,\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mpadded style="width:0.415em;" width="0.415em"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mpadded></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}\mathcal{C}\!\left(r_{i,t}^{\ell},\,\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E13Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E13Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}\begin{aligned} &amp;r_{i,t}^{\ell}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\\
&amp;\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right),\end{aligned}&amp;\begin{aligned} &amp;\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}\geq 0\ \text{and}\ r_{i,t}^{\ell}\leq 1+\varepsilon,\\[-2.0pt]
&amp;\text{or }\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}&lt;0\ \text{and}\ \\
&amp;r_{i,t}^{\ell}\geq 1-\varepsilon\end{aligned}\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mtext>or </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>and</mtext></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}\begin{aligned} &amp;r_{i,t}^{\ell}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\\
&amp;\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right),\end{aligned}&amp;\begin{aligned} &amp;\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}\geq 0\ \text{and}\ r_{i,t}^{\ell}\leq 1+\varepsilon,\\[-2.0pt]
&amp;\text{or }\hat{A}_{i,t}^{\ell}&lt;0\ \text{and}\ \\
&amp;r_{i,t}^{\ell}\geq 1-\varepsilon\end{aligned}\\
0,&amp;\text{otherwise}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.8" class="ltx_p">Substituting Eq. <a href="#A2.E13" title="In Advantage Decomposition and Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B HRPO Analysis ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> into
Eq. <a href="#A2.E11" title="In Advantage Decomposition and Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B HRPO Analysis ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> gives the time-wise policy gradient:</p>
