<tr id="A2.E14Xi" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14Xi.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg]\Bigg\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.337em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo><mo maxsize="2.600em" minsize="2.600em">]</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\,\|\,\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(\cdot\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t})\right)\Bigg]\Bigg\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.9" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{i,t}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{i,t}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary condition in the first branch of
Eq. <a href="#A2.E13" title="In Advantage Decomposition and Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B HRPO Analysis ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>; it is not a new reward or advantage
variable, but only records whether the corresponding clipped surrogate is
active. Equivalently, if no clipping is active at token <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the streaming-token
and deep-token gradient factors reduce to</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\text{s}}|}r_{i,t}^{s}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}r_{i,t}^{g}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\text{s}}|}r_{i,t}^{s}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}r_{i,t}^{g}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right),\text{for }1\leq t\leq|t_{\text{s}}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right),\text{for }1\leq t\leq|t_{\text{s}}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">and</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\text{s}}|}r_{i,t}^{d}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}r_{i,t}^{g}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|-|t_{\text{s}}|}r_{i,t}^{d}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}r_{i,t}^{g}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right),\text{for }|t_{\text{s}}|&lt;t\leq|o_{i}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>for </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cdot\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}\!\left(o_{i,t}\mid q,o_{i,&lt;t}\right),\text{for }|t_{\text{s}}|&lt;t\leq|o_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">with the KL-gradient term subtracted at every token as shown in
Eq. <a href="#A2.E14" title="In Advantage Decomposition and Policy Gradient ‣ Appendix B HRPO Analysis ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>. At <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\theta_{\mathrm{old}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>old</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\theta_{\mathrm{old}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
the ratios equal one, HRPO uses the effective per-token advantages</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\text{s}}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g},\quad\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|\!-\!|t_{\text{s}}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mtext>s</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>g</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\lambda}{|t_{\text{s}}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{s}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g},\quad\frac{\lambda}{|o_{i}|\!-\!|t_{\text{s}}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{d}+\frac{1}{|o_{i}|}\hat{A}_{i,t}^{g}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.3" class="ltx_p">for streaming and deep tokens respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Reward Analysis for Streaming Reasoning</h2>

<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Adaptive reward hacking</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">An intuitive design for local length reward is to add accuracy and format
gates, so that only correct and parseable trajectories receive the local
length signal. However, our local length term is actually a <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">penalty</em>.
Consider <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}^{s}\leq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}^{s}\leq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and the gated design
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}^{L_{s}}=R_{i}^{\mathrm{acc}}R_{i,\mathrm{fmt}}^{s}\ell_{i}^{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>acc</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>fmt</mi></mrow><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}^{L_{s}}=R_{i}^{\mathrm{acc}}R_{i,\mathrm{fmt}}^{s}\ell_{i}^{s}</annotation></semantics></math>. Correct and
format-valid samples are penalized when they are too long, while incorrect or
malformed samples are multiplied by the gate and therefore receive <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> penalty.
The gate thus creates a loophole: failing the gate can be better than being
correct but verbose.</p>
<table id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Rollout</th>
<th id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Accuracy</th>
<th id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t">Format</th>
<th id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}^{L_{s}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>s</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}^{L_{s}}</annotation></semantics></math></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">A: correct but long</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">1</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-3</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">B: incorrect</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">C: incorrect</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_b">D: incorrect</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">0</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b">1</td>
<td id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_b"><math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After group normalization, the zero-valued incorrect rollouts can obtain
positive local length advantages, while the correct long rollout obtains a
negative one. The local branch can therefore reward failed trajectories for
avoiding the length cost, creating a direct conflict with the global signal.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This failure may appear to be solvable by carefully tuning the coefficient of
the local length reward. In the gated regime, however, weighting the reward
before computing the advantage cancels the coefficient during normalization, as
shown in Eq. <a href="#A3.E19" title="In Hyperparameter Sensitivity Analysis ‣ Appendix C Reward Analysis for Streaming Reasoning ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>. Therefore, local length scores
should not be gated by final accuracy, and format validity should be handled by
masking or filtering at the advantage-computation level rather than by
multiplying the negative penalty itself.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyperparameter Sensitivity Analysis</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We analyze why HRPO applies <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> after component-wise normalization in
Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="In Hierarchical Advantage Composition ‣ 3.2 Adaptive Streaming Reasoning Reward ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Consider a reward-level alternative at any
hierarchical level <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in\{s,d,g\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in\{s,d,g\}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}^{\ell}(\beta)=b^{\ell}+\beta g^{\ell}X_{i}^{\ell},\qquad\beta&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}^{\ell}(\beta)=b^{\ell}+\beta g^{\ell}X_{i}^{\ell},\qquad\beta&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the shared additive gate reward, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\ell}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\ell}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is the shared
multiplicative gate scale, and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{i}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{i}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> is the remaining length or efficiency
shaping term. In the active gated regime, <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> are fixed within
the sampled group. The normalized advantage is therefore:</p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{A}_{i}^{\ell}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{A}_{i}^{\ell}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{R_{i}^{\ell}(\beta)-\mu\big(\{R_{j}^{\ell}(\beta)\}_{j=1}^{G}\big)}{\sigma\big(\{R_{j}^{\ell}(\beta)\}_{j=1}^{G}\big)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{R_{i}^{\ell}(\beta)-\mu\big(\{R_{j}^{\ell}(\beta)\}_{j=1}^{G}\big)}{\sigma\big(\{R_{j}^{\ell}(\beta)\}_{j=1}^{G}\big)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\beta g^{\ell}\!\left(X_{i}^{\ell}-\mu(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})\right)}{\beta g^{\ell}\sigma(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\beta g^{\ell}\!\left(X_{i}^{\ell}-\mu(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})\right)}{\beta g^{\ell}\sigma(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{X_{i}^{\ell}-\mu(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\sigma(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>j</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{X_{i}^{\ell}-\mu(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})}{\sigma(\{X_{j}^{\ell}\}_{j=1}^{G})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Thus reward-level weighting makes <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> ineffective under fixed gates. In
contrast, Eq. <a href="#S3.E8" title="In Hierarchical Advantage Composition ‣ 3.2 Adaptive Streaming Reasoning Reward ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> applies <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> after
normalization, so it remains an explicit multiplier on the composed advantage.
If a component has zero variance within the group, that component still
produces no relative advantage.
The corresponding experiments can be found at Table <a href="#A3.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Hyperparameter Weighting Experiments ‣ Appendix C Reward Analysis for Streaming Reasoning ‣ AdaSR: Adaptive Streaming Reasoning withHierarchical Relative Policy Optimization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Hyperparameter Weighting Experiments</h4>

<figure id="A3.T6" class="ltx_table">
<div id="A3.T6.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:366.8pt;vertical-align:-181.6pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-66.6pt,70.8pt) scale(0.721336948049263,0.721336948049263) ;">
